   "said": "sav-ont",
   "_said": "HER NAME IS SAID SAV-ONT, as in the old idiot savant — the one who cannot be taught and cannot be wrong about the thing she knows: the truth teller, the master of mathematics. espeak-ng (and so piper, which phonemizes through it) read the written name as savˈɑːnteɪ, sav-AHN-tay, a third syllable the name does not have; measured sˈav ˈɒnt for the respelling. So SAVANTE is in the pronunciation table (data/config/pronunciation.json, voaice-pronunciation/1 v2, a byte copy of cryptoAGI/voaice pronunciation/lexicon.json) as \"Sav ont\", and every engine's synth() applies it — the render store, /listen, the docsplayer and the browser lane alike. The page keeps the spelling; only the voice hears the respelling.",
